rities said that  it could actually happen as early as the  beginning of september but  as we said before it's it's nothing is  for sure yet of course the ukrainians  highly welcome this  initiative  they would be very happy about these  inspectors on the ground but of course  they know that they also can't perform  any miracles and they can't prevent a  possible nuclear disaster all alone we  have to keep in mind that there is  shelling in the region still on a daily  basis so it's good news it's a step  forward but it's definitely not a  breakthrough  we are also hearing reports of potential  ukrainian drone attacks on uh  territories occupied by russia what more  can you tell us about those  yeah there are  reports about new drone attacks that  have taken place in the past hours  they come just one day after reports of  explosions in occupied territory and  even  in russia  itself  officials here in ukraine don't  officially comment on these incidents  but there are some senior officials that  have hinted that  ukraine could be behind these attacks so  it obviously shows ukraine's growing  abilities to to hit  russia even far away from the front  lines and to attack  important supply lines yeah and philip  thanks so much that's jan philip schultz  reporting from odessa
 

